    "summary": "Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre has appointed new directors general for two key federal ministries, citing constitutional authority to accelerate government operations.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, September 26, 2026 — Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre of Somalia's Federal Government has appointed new directors general for several ministries, according to a statement from his office. The appointments were made under Article 119(D) of the provisional constitution, which grants the prime minister authority to hire senior civil servants.\n\nThe appointments include Abdullahi Ibrahim Abdi as Director General of the Ministry of Energy and Water Resources, and Ahmed Yusuf Abd as Director General of another ministry. The move is intended to speed up ongoing government activities, the statement said.\n\nThis is not the first time Prime Minister Barre has made such appointments. Since taking office in 2022, he has periodically reshuffled senior officials to improve efficiency. The energy and water sectors are particularly important as Somalia grapples with drought and seeks to expand access to basic services.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these appointments could affect remittance flows and investment in energy and water projects. Many diaspora members fund local initiatives in these sectors, and stable leadership is crucial for planning and partnership. The new directors general will be responsible for overseeing policy implementation and managing donor relations.\n\nObservers note that the success of these appointments will depend on how quickly the new officials can address pressing challenges, including regulatory frameworks and project coordination. The prime minister's office has not announced further details about the other appointments.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/26/%f0%9d%90%91%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%a2%f0%9d%90%a2%f0%9d%90%ac%f0%9d%90%ae%f0%9d%90%a5-%f0%9d%90%96%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%ac%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%ab%f0%9d%90%9e-%f0%9d%90%97-3/",
