    "content": "Internet and telephone services in Ethiopia's northern Tigray region have been disrupted for a fourth consecutive day, according to the internet monitoring group NetBlocks. The outage coincides with ongoing clashes between Ethiopian federal forces and Tigrayan forces, marking a significant escalation in tensions. The communications blackout has made it difficult to verify the situation on the ground independently.\n\nThe current fighting is the latest development in a long-standing conflict between the federal government and the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF), which governed Tigray before the war that began in November 2020. A peace agreement signed in November 2022 ended major combat operations, but relations have remained tense over unresolved issues such as disputed territories and the status of Tigrayan forces. The resumption of hostilities signals a potential breakdown of that ceasefire.\n\nAccording to a Reuters report citing four diplomatic sources, the TPLF has accused a company—whose name was not specified—of involvement in the communications disruption. The sources did not provide further details, and Ethiopian authorities have not commented on the allegations. The cause of the outage remains unclear, but its timing alongside the military clashes suggests a deliberate move to limit information flow.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the renewed conflict in Tigray is of particular concern due to the region's proximity to Somalia and the potential for wider instability in the Horn of Africa. Many Somalis have family and business ties across Ethiopia, and any prolonged conflict could disrupt trade routes and humanitarian corridors. Additionally, the involvement of international actors in the region may shift attention and resources away from Somalia's own security and development challenges.\n\nThe international community has yet to issue a coordinated response to the latest fighting. The African Union and United Nations have previously mediated between the parties, but no new mediation efforts have been announced. Regional observers warn that a full-scale return to war would have devastating humanitarian consequences, as Tigray is still recovering from the previous conflict.\n\nThis report was compiled from information provided by Goobjoog and Reuters.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/26/isgaarsiinta-tigray-oo-goday-iyo-dagaalka-galay-oo-maalintii-afraad/",
